    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Ranger's Guile on the attacking Primeval Herald 3/1 during combat. The opponent has 4 untapped Mountains and 4 cards in hand, meaning they could have instant-speed removal to kill the Herald. Ranger's Guile would grant hexproof protection for the most important creature on the board, deal 1 extra damage, and the player has no other use for their remaining mana this turn (only Evolving Wilds in hand, no land drops remaining).",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Ranger's Guile, dealing only 3 damage and leaving the Herald vulnerable to removal.",
      "better_line": "Cast Ranger's Guile on Primeval Herald to make it 4/2 with hexproof, dealing 4 damage and protecting it from potential instant-speed removal from the opponent's 4 cards in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 181,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 164,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Ranger's Guile preemptively in response to Chandra being cast, before knowing what Chandra's ability will target. If the opponent uses Chandra's +1 to deal 2 damage to the player's face instead of a creature, Ranger's Guile is completely wasted. Even if Chandra targets a creature, casting Guile now commits the protection to a possibly wrong creature.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Ranger's Guile in response to Chandra, Flame's Fury being cast, before any ability is activated",
      "better_line": "Let Chandra resolve, then hold Ranger's Guile to respond to whichever activated ability the opponent chooses. This way you can protect the actual targeted creature (if any) or save the card if Chandra targets the player.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 194,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 169,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to activate Evolving Wilds while Rumbling Baloth was on the stack. Evolving Wilds is a land so summoning sickness doesn't apply, and cracking it is pure upside: it thins the deck and provides an extra land for future turns at zero cost.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Evolving Wilds",
      "better_line": "Activate Evolving Wilds to fetch a basic land (likely a Mountain for color flexibility or Forest), thinning the deck and adding a land for future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 213,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 188,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "GPT53C Teach declined to attack with Affectionate Indrik 4/4 when the opponent had zero creatures, zero untapped mana, and no way to interact. This leaves 4 free damage on the table against an opponent at 17 life with Chandra (a dangerous planeswalker) about to come online. Attacking with Indrik would put the opponent to 10 instead of 14, significantly increasing pressure and the likelihood of closing the game before Chandra takes over.",
      "action_taken": "Passed on adding Affectionate Indrik (and Oashra Cultivator) to the attack, only sending Primeval Herald for 3 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with at least Affectionate Indrik alongside Primeval Herald for 7 total damage (3+4). The opponent has no blockers and no mana to interact. Oashra Cultivator attacking for 0 is irrelevant, but the Indrik's 4 damage is critical free value.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 222,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 196,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to activate Evolving Wilds during combat. With 0 cards in hand and no reason to hold it, cracking Evolving Wilds is a free action that thins the deck (improving future draws with an empty hand) and provides an extra untapped land next turn. There's no downside to activating it here.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Evolving Wilds",
      "better_line": "Activate Evolving Wilds to fetch a basic land, thinning the deck and ensuring an extra untapped land next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 223,
